  "prefLabel": "Par 303.05 Periodic Review of Medical Parole Eligibility",
  "priorExpiration": "2016-09-06",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Par 303.05 Periodic Review of Medical Parole Eligibility. The board shall request periodic medical reports regarding the condition of parolees released under the provisions of this section. If the director of forensic and medical services concludes that the parolee no longer meets the criteria for medical parole, the medical parole shall be revoked by the parole board and the offender returned to prison.\n\nSource. #9255, eff 9-6-08, EXPIRED: 9-6-16\n\nNew. #12158, eff 4-7-17",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/par100-500.html"
